{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"title":"GrafluentCollections","externalID":"GrafluentCollections","role":"collection"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import GrafluentCollections"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and can be imported on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import GrafluentCollections","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","print(scores.prefixSum(through: 3))  \/\/ 9","print(scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6))       \/\/ 19"]},{"anchor":"Values-not-references","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Values, not references"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every collection is a copy-on-write struct. Assigning one copies nothing until one of the copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is mutated; then only that copy pays, once, and the other keeps its elements:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let original: BTree = [1, 2, 3]","var copy = original","copy.insert(4)","Array(original)   \/\/ [1, 2, 3]","Array(copy)       \/\/ [1, 2, 3, 4]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices of a tree live in flat arrays linked by integer indices rather than in a class per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, so a copy is a few array copies and a traversal reads memory almost in order. The API","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"follows the standard library and Swift Collections: the sorted sets are ","type":"text"},{"code":"SetAlgebra","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random-access collections indexed by rank, the dictionaries take ","type":"text"},{"code":"subscript(_:default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range trees are collections of their values.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Traps-and-checked-spellings","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Traps and checked spellings"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A plain spelling traps when its precondition fails, like an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" subscript out of range: it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fast path, for callers who know the precondition holds. Beside it, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws a typed error instead, one of those in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":" turns it into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7]","primes[2]                    \/\/ 5","try primes[checked: 9]       \/\/ throws IndexOutOfRange"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mutation that would break a structure’s invariant, such as joining two treaps whose elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interleave, throws on its plain spelling and changes nothing. Where the standard library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collections return an optional ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a dictionary’s subscript, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"min()"},{"type":"text","text":"), these do too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Grafluent-conversions","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Grafluent conversions"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A collection whose shape is a tree converts to the Grafluent type of that shape: ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"RootedTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"PrefixTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with an initializer on the Grafluent type that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"costs O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") once. Structures whose shape is a general graph, such as decision diagrams and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automata, offer a view that is a Grafluent graph without copying. Either way, Grafluent’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms, drawings and file formats run over the collection; its own operations never go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the conversion. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","type":"reference"},{"text":" shows the round trip.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Modules","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Modules"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Group","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Modules","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Search trees"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (AVL, red–black and splay trees, treaps), "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (B-trees), "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists"},{"type":"text","text":" (skip lists)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries"},{"type":"text","text":" (tries over any sequence of symbols, radix and Patricia trees, Aho–Corasick automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Suffix structures"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/suffixstructures","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (suffix arrays with LCP, suffix trees, suffix automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decision diagrams"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"},{"type":"text","text":" (reduced ordered BDDs, zero-suppressed ZDDs)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Range and spatial trees","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (Fenwick trees, segment trees with lazy propagation, interval trees), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/spatialtrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (k-d trees, quadtrees, octrees)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sequences and persistence","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/ropes","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (ropes: sequences as balanced trees of chunks), ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (path-copying weight-balanced trees that keep every version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caches"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/caches"},{"type":"text","text":" (LRU caches)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"CollectionErrors","type":"codeVoice"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"CollectionErrors"},{"type":"text","text":": the errors the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" spellings throw, re-exported by every module that throws them"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections","title":"GrafluentCollections","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/GrafluentCollections/documentation/binarysearchtrees":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees","titleInlineContent":[{"code":"BinarySearchTrees","type":"codeVoice"}],"title":"BinarySearchTrees"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring."}],"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","title":"Tries and suffix structures"},"doc://GrafluentCollectio